WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:42.820
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:10.840 --> 02:12.860
- Tsuzuki!
- Byakko!

02:16.240 --> 02:17.900
You!

02:20.710 --> 02:23.040
You must have suffered, you little insect.

02:23.150 --> 02:26.850
You! You're still alive!

02:26.950 --> 02:29.940
You mustn't underestimate
the power of the devil.

02:32.890 --> 02:35.020
The part that I bit will start to hurt.

02:35.130 --> 02:36.290
Stop!

02:37.200 --> 02:41.890
That is because I am entering you,
each and every cell in you.

02:43.130 --> 02:46.970
Look, my mark will soon reveal itself on you.

02:48.170 --> 02:50.610
Of the black sheep.

02:50.710 --> 02:53.940
The mark that turns its back on God.

02:55.180 --> 02:57.550
You should feel lucky

02:57.650 --> 03:02.180
that you were chosen
to become a part of my body.

03:05.520 --> 03:07.510
Poor little lamb.

03:10.520 --> 03:15.520
Episode 6: Devil's Trill, Part 3

03:17.000 --> 03:19.030
Wow! Amazing!

03:38.260 --> 03:40.190
So where do we go next?

03:40.290 --> 03:43.230
- You still want to go sightseeing?
- Of course!

03:43.330 --> 03:46.590
There're a lot of tourist sights in Amakusa.

03:52.140 --> 03:53.760
That feels good!

03:54.040 --> 03:55.970
Tsuzuki should've come too.

03:56.070 --> 03:58.700
He has a lot of loose ends to tie up.

03:58.810 --> 04:02.440
Too bad. I wanted to
thank him for saving me

04:02.550 --> 04:05.070
by maybe buying him
a big seafood dinner.

04:05.180 --> 04:09.280
Yeah. It's unlike him to turn down a meal.

04:09.390 --> 04:10.620
Hey, Hisoka?

04:11.520 --> 04:15.580
You were saying the other day
that kindness can be a weakness.

04:15.860 --> 04:19.920
But I'm really grateful for his kindness.

04:20.030 --> 04:22.630
The fact that both Kazusa and I are alive

04:22.730 --> 04:25.730
is because you guys protected us.

04:26.540 --> 04:28.510
Do we go our separate ways tomorrow?

04:28.610 --> 04:29.800
Yeah.

04:30.740 --> 04:32.440
I see.

04:34.950 --> 04:38.210
You sure like to put in the hours.

04:38.480 --> 04:42.440
It's crazy you have to work so late.
On a Sunday, no less.

04:42.890 --> 04:45.550
Do you have some job
you're right in the middle of?

04:45.660 --> 04:48.460
Yes. I have a lot to catch up on.

04:48.560 --> 04:50.490
You sure are a hard worker.

04:51.400 --> 04:52.690
Here it is.

04:54.030 --> 04:56.060
Here you go.
The cleaver you were looking for.

04:56.170 --> 04:57.460
Thanks very much.

04:57.570 --> 05:00.500
What are you going to be using this for?

05:00.610 --> 05:03.040
Oh, it's not for anything important.

05:03.640 --> 05:08.140
I just want to get rid of
a small unsightly branch.

05:11.650 --> 05:13.280
You're back, Tsuzuki.

05:13.380 --> 05:15.440
I just put on some tea.

05:16.520 --> 05:19.180
- Isn't Kazusa here with you?
- Kazusa?

05:19.290 --> 05:22.620
I told you before that Kazusa's
at the Ju-Oh-Cho until tomorrow.

05:22.730 --> 05:24.590
Oh, right.

05:24.700 --> 05:29.100
Tsuzuki! I picked up
some spicy squid for Boss.

05:29.200 --> 05:31.330
- You think that's all right?
- Sure. Why not?

05:31.440 --> 05:34.560
Boss doesn't like sweets,
so that's why I got it.

05:34.670 --> 05:36.770
Good. Good thinking.

05:36.880 --> 05:39.240
Well, I'm going to go take a bath.

05:39.340 --> 05:41.570
Then you'll need a change of clothes.

05:45.420 --> 05:46.710
Hisoka?

05:55.230 --> 05:59.490
Do you still want to fight me
even after all this time?

05:59.600 --> 06:03.190
You're not being very nice, Tsuzuki.

06:05.670 --> 06:10.440
No matter how much you fight,
your body is under my control.

06:10.540 --> 06:13.600
You do what I say.

06:14.280 --> 06:16.040
The ones whom you love

06:16.150 --> 06:18.950
shall be killed by your own hands.

06:37.400 --> 06:38.990
Tsuzuki.

06:39.100 --> 06:41.090
Look. The immortal light.

06:41.210 --> 06:45.540
They say the immortal light is
the spirit of those who died at sea.

06:45.740 --> 06:47.340
Isn't it beautiful?

06:48.550 --> 06:50.480
Don't I get any thanks?

06:50.780 --> 06:53.310
Thanks for protecting you from the devil?

06:53.420 --> 06:55.410
Oh, right. Thank you.

06:55.520 --> 06:58.460
That's no good.
You think that's enough?

06:58.560 --> 07:00.250
Then what should I do?

07:00.360 --> 07:02.020
What would you like for me to do?

07:02.130 --> 07:04.090
If there's anything I can do for you?

07:04.400 --> 07:06.260
Anything?

07:07.330 --> 07:10.560
Then I want to take your body.

07:11.370 --> 07:13.770
W-Wait a minute!
Is this some kind of joke?!

07:16.040 --> 07:19.270
I want you to give me your life!

07:34.490 --> 07:36.460
You're beautiful, Hijiri.

07:37.160 --> 07:41.620
The crimson red of your blood
suits your creamy white skin.

07:49.110 --> 07:51.230
It's a full moon.

07:57.080 --> 08:01.210
That's the end of our contract, Minase Hijiri.

08:04.660 --> 08:06.020
What?!

08:06.120 --> 08:07.350
Is that true?

08:07.460 --> 08:09.360
- Yes.
- What?!

08:09.460 --> 08:11.830
I checked all over his body!

08:11.930 --> 08:15.230
The devil must've gradually
messed with his mind.

08:15.330 --> 08:19.360
First of all, I'm sure that
Tsuzuki is possessed by the devil.

08:19.470 --> 08:20.630
Do you have any proof?

08:20.740 --> 08:23.610
I couldn't feel his emotions at all.

08:23.710 --> 08:26.300
They usually come through bright and loud.

08:26.880 --> 08:28.940
He's completely empty.

08:29.810 --> 08:30.780
Besides...

08:30.880 --> 08:35.110
he didn't even remember that
Boss has an incredible sweet tooth.

08:37.960 --> 08:39.620
What the--

08:45.630 --> 08:48.790
Where are you, Kazusa?!
Come on out!

08:48.900 --> 08:50.330
Stop it, Tsuzuki!

08:50.440 --> 08:52.730
You're being controlled by the devil!

08:52.840 --> 08:54.670
Hijiri's dead.

08:54.770 --> 08:58.940
The contract states that I am to get Kazusa.

09:01.580 --> 09:03.710
Don't go around killing people.

09:03.820 --> 09:06.250
I'm still alive, Sargatanas.

09:06.350 --> 09:07.510
That's crazy!

09:07.620 --> 09:09.610
I know I killed you with my own hands!

09:09.720 --> 09:13.250
Yes. You did indeed kill me.

09:13.520 --> 09:15.860
But one thing you're wrong about is that

09:15.960 --> 09:20.330
the one you killed was me;
I had taken the place of Hijiri.

09:20.430 --> 09:21.630
What?!

09:23.470 --> 09:24.440
Don't worry.

09:24.540 --> 09:28.340
We'll be all right.
He did say we'd be safe here, right?

09:28.440 --> 09:30.840
To kill a contractor is the worst crime

09:30.940 --> 09:33.740
that you can commit in the netherworld.

09:33.850 --> 09:36.280
This is it for you, Sargatanas.

09:42.690 --> 09:46.890
To think you'd mess with me,
the leader of the wandering spirits.

09:46.990 --> 09:49.690
I'm rather impressed, kid.

09:50.060 --> 09:53.190
Now that it's come to this,
the contract is irrelevant.

09:53.300 --> 09:55.600
I will kill Kazusa as soon as I find her.

09:55.700 --> 09:57.760
And then you'll be next.

10:00.840 --> 10:04.300
I'll have you experience
the torment of hell first.

10:04.410 --> 10:05.670
And then I'll kill you.

10:09.450 --> 10:11.010
<i>To all departments...</i>

10:11.120 --> 10:14.240
<i>raise the defense shield
and prepare for attack!</i>

10:15.390 --> 10:17.410
What a mess this has turned out to be.

10:17.890 --> 10:21.760
We're not going to have much of
a chance against those from hell.

10:21.860 --> 10:26.390
And I don't know if we have the
time to summon other Shinigami.

10:27.070 --> 10:28.660
Boss!

10:37.180 --> 10:38.610
Kazusa.

10:38.710 --> 10:41.040
I want you to wait here.
All right?

10:41.380 --> 10:42.680
Hi-chan!

10:43.680 --> 10:47.280
Let's use the Reibaku to
separate the devil from Tsuzuki!

10:47.390 --> 10:50.150
N-No... No way!
It's too dangerous!

10:50.250 --> 10:54.690
That spell is too powerful
and may damage his psyche!

10:54.830 --> 10:56.920
If you fail, the spell will bounce back to you!

10:57.030 --> 11:00.000
Then are you saying that we
should just stand by and watch?!

11:00.100 --> 11:01.930
I don't think he'd want the humiliation

11:02.030 --> 11:04.500
of being manipulated by the devil,

11:04.600 --> 11:07.300
and being forced to kill his own friends!

11:07.810 --> 11:11.210
We'll have to take a chance
on his ability to withstand it.

11:13.210 --> 11:15.200
All right.
You have my approval.

11:20.890 --> 11:22.250
Where are you hiding?!

11:22.950 --> 11:25.250
Come on out, Kazusa!

11:26.050 --> 11:30.050
<i>Rin pyou tou sha kai jin retsu zai zen!</i>

11:31.060 --> 11:32.260
Reibaku!

11:41.210 --> 11:43.000
- Stop it!
- Hijiri!

11:43.110 --> 11:46.080
If you go any further,
you'll damage Tsuzuki forever!

11:46.180 --> 11:50.740
But at this rate, he'll be possessed
by the devil for eternity!

11:50.850 --> 11:51.870
B-But--

11:51.980 --> 11:53.110
We have no choice.

11:53.220 --> 11:55.690
I want to save Tsuzuki too!

12:03.430 --> 12:06.690
Is he going to try to break the Reibaku?!

12:06.860 --> 12:10.160
Oh, no! It's because the seal isn't complete.

12:10.270 --> 12:15.210
Tsuzuki's power is starting
to overwhelm the kid's!

12:17.940 --> 12:19.740
Watch it, Hijiri!

12:21.250 --> 12:22.870
- Hijiri!
- Kid!

12:23.450 --> 12:27.950
Yami no Matsuei

12:30.220 --> 12:33.190
Kid, I will never forgive you.

12:34.330 --> 12:38.320
Your wretched Shinigami
have tried me twice now.

12:39.300 --> 12:41.360
Call this a parting gift.

12:41.900 --> 12:46.340
I'll kill you using the power of
Tsuzuki, whom you tried to protect.

12:46.440 --> 12:49.500
Shut up! When are you
going to cut out that attitude?

12:50.070 --> 12:51.840
Now is the time for you to be judged

12:51.940 --> 12:54.170
not by God, but by humans.

12:54.280 --> 12:55.680
- Kid!
- Kurosaki-kun!

12:56.080 --> 12:58.310
I'm not going to let you kill me!

12:58.420 --> 13:01.250
Yeah! We're going to try to save Tsuzuki!

13:01.990 --> 13:03.420
Save?

13:04.760 --> 13:06.880
Do you really think this man is worthy

13:06.990 --> 13:10.590
of all the effort you intend
on taking to save him?

13:10.700 --> 13:13.860
The black sheep who was forsaken by God?

13:14.200 --> 13:17.690
Don't tell me you've even
looked into his memories?!

13:17.800 --> 13:19.360
Well, of course.

13:19.900 --> 13:21.500
Everything. All of it.

13:22.370 --> 13:23.470
Kid! You all right?!

13:24.880 --> 13:27.280
I can feel it.
Tsuzuki's consciousness!

13:27.610 --> 13:31.210
It was easy possessing this guy.

13:31.320 --> 13:33.650
As soon as I showed him
the events of that night

13:33.750 --> 13:35.340
he gave in quite easily.

13:35.950 --> 13:36.940
Stop it!

13:37.360 --> 13:39.880
Right now, he's about to lose his sanity

13:39.990 --> 13:43.720
as he is being forced to
relive his crimes over and over.

13:43.830 --> 13:48.890
He can't stop or escape from the
alternate world I created for him.

13:49.300 --> 13:50.270
Until he dies

13:50.370 --> 13:53.360
he will continue to relive
the crimes that he committed!

13:53.470 --> 13:54.460
Don't do it!

13:54.570 --> 13:56.840
Don't torment Tsuzuki anymore!

13:56.940 --> 13:58.530
Who's the one who ought to be judged?!

13:58.640 --> 14:01.110
Me? Don't make me laugh!

14:01.680 --> 14:07.550
Mere humans can't save him!
Not this forsaken, filthy soul!

14:08.420 --> 14:10.410
You're not one to give up, are you?

14:10.520 --> 14:12.650
Try as you may, it'll never work on me.

14:12.760 --> 14:16.220
Then I'll keep trying until it works!

14:27.040 --> 14:28.340
The fool!

14:28.440 --> 14:30.240
Don't you understand that it won't work

14:30.340 --> 14:33.500
no matter how many times
you cast your spell!?

14:33.610 --> 14:36.510
Tsuzuki!
Come back, Tsuzuki!

14:36.610 --> 14:38.480
Come back to us!

14:42.320 --> 14:44.950
I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

14:45.390 --> 14:47.050
<i>Why did you kill me?</i>

14:47.660 --> 14:49.420
<i>I'm hurting!</i>

14:51.130 --> 14:54.220
<i>No! I don't want to die!</i>

14:55.270 --> 14:56.530
Forgive me!

14:57.900 --> 15:02.930
I did whatever I was able to.
That was the best I could do!

15:07.580 --> 15:11.480
Where are you running to,
the one who wears my mark?

15:11.580 --> 15:14.070
There is nowhere you can run to.

15:14.190 --> 15:16.380
No one will forgive you.

15:16.490 --> 15:19.750
They hate you.
They despise you.

15:23.860 --> 15:25.020
I like you.

15:25.460 --> 15:28.230
I really like you.

15:28.730 --> 15:30.600
You did protect me after all.

15:30.700 --> 15:31.830
Hijiri.

15:31.940 --> 15:33.230
How can this be?

15:33.340 --> 15:36.000
This is not one of my illusions.

15:36.110 --> 15:37.800
Where did it come from?

15:40.680 --> 15:43.580
Don't think too much about the past.

15:43.680 --> 15:45.650
What's important is now.

15:46.250 --> 15:50.080
You saved me.
That's more than enough.

15:50.650 --> 15:54.320
So you've got to come back.
Back to us.

16:01.800 --> 16:03.060
Wh-What?!

16:03.170 --> 16:05.190
There's a crack in my alternate world!

16:05.300 --> 16:09.530
Does Tsuzuki think he can escape
from the darkness of his soul?

16:09.910 --> 16:13.810
How much longer are you going to
be messing around, Tsuzuki?

16:14.250 --> 16:16.440
Don't hesitate before the devil!

16:17.050 --> 16:20.480
Get up! Show me the
power of your darkness!

16:26.960 --> 16:28.050
What the--

16:28.160 --> 16:31.860
I see. This was your work, Lord of Hades!

16:40.770 --> 16:43.040
He's coming!
The Reibaku worked!

16:48.410 --> 16:50.900
A human defeats the devil...

16:53.680 --> 16:54.650
Tsuzuki!

16:55.050 --> 16:59.220
You! You're nothing but insects!

16:59.920 --> 17:04.160
I'll crush you all!

17:09.770 --> 17:11.100
Hijiri.

17:21.550 --> 17:22.530
Hijiri!

17:22.810 --> 17:25.040
Hi-chan!

17:25.520 --> 17:27.040
Kazusa!

17:39.300 --> 17:40.990
What did the Lord have to say?

17:41.100 --> 17:42.430
In regard to this

17:42.530 --> 17:44.660
he said he finds no fault in Tsuzuki,

17:44.770 --> 17:49.070
who was possessed by the devil
through a parasite in his body.

17:49.170 --> 17:51.000
That's a relief.

17:51.510 --> 17:52.600
Yeah.

17:54.510 --> 17:56.480
Hey, you're awake, Hijiri.

17:59.920 --> 18:01.910
It's all over now, Hijiri.

18:02.420 --> 18:03.510
Everything.

18:03.620 --> 18:04.920
I see.

18:05.020 --> 18:06.320
Where's Kazusa?

18:06.420 --> 18:08.760
Kazusa died.

18:09.030 --> 18:11.720
She was crushed by that collapsing pillar.

18:13.000 --> 18:13.990
I see.

18:17.330 --> 18:21.100
Aren't you going to see me off, Tsuzuki?

18:21.310 --> 18:26.800
Well, I'm not sure I can even
face you with all that's happened.

18:27.480 --> 18:32.440
I tried to kill you guys after
saying that I'd protect you.

18:32.920 --> 18:35.720
You didn't need to protect me.

18:36.190 --> 18:38.590
You didn't have to protect me.

18:38.960 --> 18:42.650
So go a little easier on yourself
for your own sake.

18:42.760 --> 18:44.130
Hijiri.

18:48.500 --> 18:50.970
You'll come to my concert, right?

18:51.070 --> 18:54.500
I'll try to play the Devil's Trill properly.

18:55.340 --> 18:57.810
I'll be sure to play it well.

19:02.310 --> 19:04.250
Did Hijiri already go?

19:04.350 --> 19:08.810
I told you. You should never be
casual about making promises.

19:08.950 --> 19:10.920
You're right about that.

19:11.020 --> 19:13.320
I wasn't able to keep my promise.

19:14.190 --> 19:16.060
What a contradiction I am.

19:16.160 --> 19:19.100
To think I'm a Shinigami,
guilty of having killed people

19:19.200 --> 19:22.170
but who still wants to protect people.

19:23.100 --> 19:27.660
But I had no intention of lying.

19:27.770 --> 19:30.330
I really wanted to protect those two.

19:30.940 --> 19:33.640
You may not believe that.

19:33.740 --> 19:35.010
I know.

19:35.110 --> 19:39.610
We all know that you take
things seriously all the time.

19:39.720 --> 19:43.850
Don't get all hung up on
petty little things, you fool.

20:25.760 --> 20:27.990
Hi-chan's amazing!

20:28.100 --> 20:31.330
The Devil's Trill is actually
quite a beautiful piece.

20:31.440 --> 20:37.240
Yeah. The most beautiful and
most difficult created by the devil.

20:37.910 --> 20:40.900
It was the music brought
to people by angels

20:41.010 --> 20:44.610
banished from heaven
for an act of treason against God.

20:45.180 --> 20:48.950
To play the music of the devil
was seen as an act of betrayal.

20:57.660 --> 20:59.250
Good job, Hijiri!

20:59.360 --> 21:02.560
- That was really great!
- Thanks!

21:05.570 --> 21:08.500
- What's this?
- There's no name on it.

21:08.610 --> 21:09.940
What a fool.

21:10.040 --> 21:13.480
I see. He did come.

21:18.080 --> 21:20.480
You didn't come to see me

21:20.980 --> 21:24.320
because you knew
that we would meet again.

21:24.690 --> 21:26.520
Am I right?

21:27.490 --> 21:30.090
Wherever you all may be,
my precious friends

21:30.190 --> 21:34.560
the music I play from
now on will all be for you.

21:39.960 --> 21:42.960
Next Episode

21:41.670 --> 21:42.870
The serial murders that

21:42.970 --> 21:44.740
take place on a luxury liner.

21:44.840 --> 21:47.740
A prophesy of murder
hidden in the tarot cards.

21:47.850 --> 21:51.940
Resting his bones on a cruise ship?
Tatsumi sure plans things his way.

21:52.050 --> 21:55.990
Sorry. I'll leave you guys to
figure out how to storm the ship.

21:56.090 --> 21:58.320
Oh, right. It was still work.

22:00.260 --> 22:09.910
Episode 7     The King of Swords, Part 1

22:00.260 --> 22:04.130
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The King of Swords, Part 1 .

22:05.460 --> 22:08.330
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
